# One checked affine transform serves shader instances, normals and local picking.
import scene_camera.dl

class:
    patterns:
        UI scene transform
    members:
        matrix as graphics matrix
        inverse as graphics matrix
        handedness as a floating-point number

to get [the UI scene vector] {vector:value} [multiplied by] {graphics matrix:matrix} [translated] {boolean:translated}:
    set converted to the UI scene vector form of value
    set x to the x of converted
    set y to the y of converted
    set z to the z of converted
    set horizontal to (the item at 0 in matrix) * x + (the item at 4 in matrix) * y + (the item at 8 in matrix) * z
    set vertical to (the item at 1 in matrix) * x + (the item at 5 in matrix) * y + (the item at 9 in matrix) * z
    set depth to (the item at 2 in matrix) * x + (the item at 6 in matrix) * y + (the item at 10 in matrix) * z
    if translated:
        set horizontal to horizontal + (the item at 12 in matrix)
        set vertical to vertical + (the item at 13 in matrix)
        set depth to depth + (the item at 14 in matrix)
    return a new vector with x horizontal, y vertical and z depth

to get [a UI scene transform from] {graphics matrix:matrix}:
    for each component in matrix:
        require condition (component is finite) reporting "Scene transforms require finite matrix components"
    require condition (((the item at 3 in matrix) = 0.0) and (((the item at 7 in matrix) = 0.0) and (((the item at 11 in matrix) = 0.0) and ((the item at 15 in matrix) = 1.0)))) reporting "Scene model transforms must be affine"
    set first to the UI scene vector form of (a new vector with x (the item at 0 in matrix), y (the item at 1 in matrix) and z (the item at 2 in matrix))
    set second to the UI scene vector form of (a new vector with x (the item at 4 in matrix), y (the item at 5 in matrix) and z (the item at 6 in matrix))
    set third to the UI scene vector form of (a new vector with x (the item at 8 in matrix), y (the item at 9 in matrix) and z (the item at 10 in matrix))
    set cofactor to the cross product of second and third
    set determinant to the dot product of first and cofactor
    require condition (determinant != 0.0) reporting "Scene model transforms must be invertible"
    set rows to [cofactor / determinant, (the cross product of third and first) / determinant, (the cross product of first and second) / determinant]
    set translation to the UI scene vector form of (a new vector with x (the item at 12 in matrix), y (the item at 13 in matrix) and z (the item at 14 in matrix))
    set inverse to an identity graphics matrix
    set index to 0
    for each row in rows:
        store ((the x of row) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into inverse at index
        store ((the y of row) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into inverse at (index + 4)
        store ((the z of row) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into inverse at (index + 8)
        store ((0.0 - the dot product of row and translation) as a 32 bit floating-point number) into inverse at (index + 12)
        increment index
    for each component in inverse:
        require condition (component is finite) reporting "Scene transform inverses must fit in float32"
    set handedness to 1.0
    if determinant < 0.0:
        set handedness to -1.0
    return @intrinsic("construct", UI scene transform, matrix, inverse, handedness)

the UI scene position of {vector:point} through {UI scene transform:transform} means: the UI scene vector point multiplied by (transform's matrix) translated true
the UI scene direction of {vector:direction} through {UI scene transform:transform} means: the UI scene vector direction multiplied by (transform's matrix) translated false
the UI scene position of {vector:point} restored through {UI scene transform:transform} means: the UI scene vector point multiplied by (transform's inverse) translated true

to get [the UI scene normal vector of] {vector:normal} [through] {UI scene transform:transform}:
    set converted to the UI scene vector form of normal
    set inverse to transform's inverse
    set x to the x of converted
    set y to the y of converted
    set z to the z of converted
    set horizontal to (the item at 0 in inverse) * x + (the item at 1 in inverse) * y + (the item at 2 in inverse) * z
    set vertical to (the item at 4 in inverse) * x + (the item at 5 in inverse) * y + (the item at 6 in inverse) * z
    set depth to (the item at 8 in inverse) * x + (the item at 9 in inverse) * y + (the item at 10 in inverse) * z
    return a new vector with x horizontal, y vertical and z depth

to get [the UI scene normal of] {vector:normal} [through] {UI scene transform:transform}:
    set result to the UI scene normal vector of normal through transform
    set magnitude to the length of result
    require condition ((magnitude is finite) and (magnitude > 0.0)) reporting "Scene normals must be finite nonzero directions"
    return result / magnitude
